    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents the cost of inlining a function. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This supports special values for functions which should &quot;always&quot; or &quot;never&quot; be inlined. Otherwise, the cost represents a unitless amount; smaller values increase the likelihood of the function being inlined.</para>
<para>Objects of this type also provide the adjusted threshold for inlining based on the information available for a particular callsite. They can be directly tested to determine if inlining should occur given the cost and threshold for this cost metric. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
